        "id": 713,
        "name": "Full Moon Party Thailand",
        "brief": "World-Famous Moonlight Beach Party",
        "description": "**Full Moon Party Thailand** is the world’s most famous beach rave, held every month on **Haad Rin Beach, Koh Phangan**, during the full moon night. Known globally for its all-night beach celebration, the **Full Moon Party Koh Phangan** attracts **30,000+ partygoers** from around the world for a night of music, neon lights, and sunrise dancing.\n\nStretching across the entire shoreline, the **Haad Rin Beach party** features multiple sound zones playing EDM, techno, psytrance, hip-hop, reggae, and house music. From **UV body paint** and **fire shows** to iconic **bucket drinks**, the Full Moon Party is a bucket-list nightlife experience for young travellers visiting Thailand.\n\nThis guide covers everything you need to know about the **Koh Phangan Full Moon Party**, including party highlights, **Full Moon Party dates**, how to reach Haad Rin, safety tips, and accommodation advice.\n\n\n### Why Attend Full Moon Party Thailand\n### \n- The **world’s most legendary beach party**\n- Takes place on **Haad Rin Beach, Koh Phangan**\n- 30+ beach bars and sound systems\n- Iconic **Full Moon Party UV paint** culture\n- Fire rope skipping and **Haad Rin fire shows Thailand**\n- All-night party ending with **sunrise beach rave Phangan**\n\nFor Indian travellers looking to experience Thailand’s nightlife scene, the Full Moon Party is an unmatched, high-energy celebration.\n\n### Full Moon Party Thailand Location & Background\n### \n📍 **Haad Rin Beach**, Koh Phangan\n- Held monthly on the night of the full moon\n- Started in the 1980s as a small beach gathering\n\nToday, the **Full Moon Party Koh Phangan** is a global phenomenon and one of the biggest recurring beach festivals in the world.\n\n\n### Party Highlights and Bucket Culture\n### \nThe Full Moon Party is known for its unique beach-party elements.\n\n#### UV Paint, Fire Shows and 30 Bars\n#### \nWhat makes the party iconic:\n\n- Neon **UV body paint** stalls everywhere\n- **Bucket drinks Full Moon Party** culture (cocktails in plastic buckets)\n- Over **30 bars along Haad Rin Beach**\n- Live DJs across multiple music zones\n- **Fire dancers and rope skipping** on the beach\n- Non-stop music until sunrise\n\nThe **Full Moon Party bars Koh Phangan** are spread across the beach, allowing partygoers to move between music styles.\n\n\n### Full Moon Party Dates\n### \n**Full Moon Party dates** depend on lunar cycles and local regulations.\n\n✔️ Held once every month\n\n✔️ Dates may shift if they clash with Buddhist holidays\n\nTravellers searching for **Full Moon Party** should always confirm closer to travel, as official dates are released annually.\n\n\n### How to Reach Haad Rin Beach, Koh Phangan\n### \n**Step-by-step access:**\n\n- Fly to **Koh Samui**\n- Take a ferry to **Koh Phangan**\n- Use taxi boats or songthaews to reach **Haad Rin Beach**\n\nMost travellers search **how to reach Haad Rin Koh Phangan ferry**, as ferries run late on party nights to accommodate crowds.\n\nExplore all Thailand Itineraries here!\n\n### Best Time to Arrive & Party Flow\n### \n- Arrive in Haad Rin by **evening (6–7 PM)**\n- Party peaks between **10 PM – 3 AM**\n- Sunrise vibes from **5:30 AM onwards**\n\nThe **sunrise beach rave in Phangan** is considered one of the most memorable moments of the night.\n\n\n### Safety, Accommodation and Pre-Parties\n### \n#### Safety Tips:\n#### \n- Drink responsibly (bucket drinks are strong)\n- Avoid swimming at night\n- Wear footwear (broken glass is common)\n- Keep valuables waterproof and secure\n\n#### Accommodation:\n#### \n- Book early if travelling during Full Moon\n- Many travellers **book Koh Phangan accommodation for Full Moon** weeks in advance\n- Stay near Haad Rin or in quieter areas with transport access\n\nComparing experiences, **Full Moon Party vs Half Moon Party**—Full Moon is massive and chaotic, while Half Moon is smaller and more organised.\n\n\n### Who Should Attend Full Moon Party Thailand\n### \n- Solo travellers\n- Groups of friends\n- Party-focused backpackers\n- Young couples looking for nightlife experiences\n\nNot ideal for families or travellers seeking quiet beach holidays.\n\n\n### Experience Full Moon Party Thailand with India Tour Expeditions\n### \nAt **India Tour Expeditions**, we help Indian travellers plan Thailand nightlife trips smoothly.\n\n✔️ Koh Phangan Full Moon Party planning\n\n✔️ Ferry coordination from Koh Samui\n\n✔️ Koh Samui–Phangan island combinations\n\n✔️ Thailand party itineraries from India\n\n🌕 Add the **Full Moon Party Thailand** to your Thailand itinerary and experience the world’s most iconic beach rave.\n",
        "slug": "full-moon-party-thailand",
