        "id": 707,
        "name": "James Bond Island",
        "brief": "Famous Limestone Island in Phang Nga Bay",
        "description": "**James Bond Island Thailand**, officially known as **Khao Phing Kan**, is one of the most iconic landmarks in **Phang Nga Bay**. Made famous by the James Bond movie *The Man with the Golden Gun*, this dramatic island features towering limestone cliffs and the instantly recognisable **Ko Tapu James Bond Rock** rising vertically from emerald-green waters.\n\nLocated inside **Ao Phang Nga National Park**, **James Bond Island Phuket tour** experiences are among the most popular day trips from Phuket and Krabi. The island is typically visited as part of a scenic boat journey through Phang Nga Bay, often combined with sea cave canoeing, floating villages, and nearby islands.\n\nThis guide covers everything you need to know about planning a **James Bond Island day trip from Phuket or Krabi**, including why it’s famous, what to expect, tour options, best time to visit, and national park fees.\n\n### Why James Bond Island Is Famous\n### \n- Iconic **James Bond movie filming location**\n- Home to the legendary **Ko Tapu limestone pillar**\n- One of Thailand’s most photographed natural landmarks\n- Stunning **limestone karst cliffs Phang Nga Bay**\n- Easy day trip from Phuket or Krabi\n- Part of a protected national park\n\nFor Indian travellers, James Bond Island is a must-see attraction combining cinema history and dramatic natural scenery.\n\n\n### James Bond Island Location & Background\n### \n📍 Located in **Phang Nga Bay**, southern Thailand\n- Official island name: **Khao Phing Kan**\n- Part of **Ao Phang Nga National Park**\n\nThe name “Phing Kan” means *leaning hills*, referring to the distinctive rock formations on the island.\n\n\n### “The Man with the Golden Gun” Filming Location\n### \nJames Bond Island rose to global fame after appearing in the 1974 film *The Man with the Golden Gun*.\n\n#### Movie Legacy and Global Recognition\n#### \nKey highlights:\n\n- Featured as Scaramanga’s hideout\n- The iconic **Ko Tapu James Bond Rock** became a global symbol\n- Transformed a quiet island into an international attraction\n- Continues to attract movie fans and travellers worldwide\n\n The **James Bond movie Man with the Golden Gun location** remains one of Thailand’s most recognisable film sites.\n\n\n#### Scenery – Limestone Cliffs, Ko Tapu Rock and Phang Nga Bay Views\n#### \nWhat makes the island visually striking:\n\n- Vertical limestone karst formations\n- Emerald waters surrounding the cliffs\n- The famous needle-shaped **Ko Tapu rock**\n- Boardwalks and viewpoints for photos\n- Calm bay waters ideal for boat exploration\n\nThe scenery around **Khao Phing Kan Phang Nga Bay** is best enjoyed from both land and water.\n\nMajestic Thailand Itinerary by India Tour Expeditions\n\n### Tours from Phuket and Krabi\n### \nJames Bond Island is visited via guided boat tours.\n\n#### Boats, Canoes and Floating Villages\n#### \nMost tours include:\n\n- Speedboat or **scenic longtail boat tour Phang Nga**\n- **Sea cave canoeing Phang Nga Bay**\n- Visit to **floating Muslim village Koh Panyee**\n- Multiple island and mangrove stops\n- Lunch and transfers (on select tours)\n\nPopular options include **James Bond Island and Hong Island canoe tours** for a more complete Phang Nga Bay experience.\n\n### Best Time to Visit James Bond Island\n### \n**Best Time of Day:**\n\n✔️ Early morning (before peak crowds)\n\n**Best Season:**\n\n✔️ November to April (dry season)\n\nMany travellers search **best time to visit James Bond Island avoid crowds**, as midday tours tend to be busy.\n\nBook your Thailand Tour now!\n\n### James Bond Island Entrance Fee (National Park)\n### \n**National Park Fee:**\n\n✔️ Approx. **300 Baht per adult**\n\nThis fee is paid to **Phang Nga Bay National Park** and helps protect the ecosystem.\n\n\n### Is James Bond Island Worth Visiting\n### \n**Yes—if you plan it right.**\n\n- Crowded but visually stunning\n- Best experienced as part of a broader Phang Nga Bay tour\n- Ideal for photography and first-time visitors\n- Short stop, but memorable scenery\n\nMany travellers ask **is James Bond Island worth visiting crowded but scenic**—the answer is yes, especially with an early or well-planned tour.\n\n\n\n### Tips for Visiting James Bond Island\n### \n- Visit early to avoid crowds\n- Wear comfortable footwear for boardwalks\n- Carry sun protection\n- Follow park rules (no climbing rocks)\n- Combine with canoeing for a better experience\n\n### Explore James Bond Island with India Tour Expeditions\n### \nAt **India Tour Expeditions**, we curate scenic Phang Nga Bay tours for Indian travellers.\n\n✔️ **James Bond Island tour from Phuket or Krabi**\n\n✔️ Canoeing and island-combo experiences\n\n✔️ National park visits with transfers\n\n✔️ Thailand tour packages from India\n\n🏝️ Add **James Bond Island Thailand (Khao Phing Kan)** to your Thailand itinerary and witness one of the world’s most iconic natural movie landmarks.",
