        "id": 708,
        "name": "Tiger Kingdom",
        "brief": "Wildlife Park Offering Close Encounters with Tigers",
        "description": "**Tiger Kingdom Phuket** is one of the most talked-about wildlife attractions in Thailand, offering visitors a rare chance to **get close to tigers** under supervised conditions. Located in **Kathu**, between Patong and Phuket Town, Tiger Kingdom allows guests to **pet, feed, and take photos with tigers** ranging from playful cubs to full-grown adults.\n\nThe experience is carefully managed by trained handlers, making it popular with families, couples, and travellers looking for a unique wildlife encounter in Phuket. Many visitors compare **Tiger Kingdom Phuket vs Tiger Kingdom Chiang Mai**, and Phuket’s location makes it especially convenient to combine with Patong sightseeing.\n\nThis guide covers **Tiger Kingdom Thailand tickets**, tiger zones, safety rules, ethical notes, best time to visit, and transfer options.\n\n\n### Why Visit Tiger Kingdom Phuket\n### \n- Rare opportunity to **see tigers up close**\n- Choose interactions with **different tiger sizes**\n- Trained handlers present at all times\n- Well-organised **photo opportunities**\n- Convenient location near Patong & Kathu\n- Short, structured visit (2–3 hours)\n\nFor Indian travellers, **Tiger Kingdom Phuket** is often a once-in-a-lifetime experience — especially for photography lovers.\n\n\n### Tiger Zones – Smallest, Medium, Big, White & Cheetah\n### \nOne of the main highlights is choosing which tiger zones you want to visit.\n**Tiger Interaction Zones**\n\n- 🐯 **Smallest / Cubs** – Short interaction time, very popular\n- 🐅 **Medium Tigers** – Balanced experience\n- 🐯 **Big Tigers** – Calm, majestic adults\n- 🤍 **White Tigers** – Rare and highly photogenic\n- 🐆 **Cheetah Zone** – Limited interaction, fast but elegant\n\nVisitors often book **Tiger Kingdom packages** that include multiple zones for a fuller experience.\n\n\n### Packages, Feeding Times & Photo Tips\n### \n **Tiger Kingdom Phuket Packages Include:**\n\n- Entry to selected tiger zones\n- Supervised interaction time\n- Professional photography assistance (own phone/camera allowed)\n- Optional feeding sessions\n\n **Opening Hours:**\n\n✔️ Daily: **9:00 AM – 6:00 PM**\n\n**Best Time to Visit:**\n\n- Morning hours are ideal\n- Tigers are more active around feeding time\n- Many search **best time Tiger Kingdom Phuket morning feeding**\n\n **Photo Tips:**\n\n- Wear bright solid colours\n- Follow handler instructions strictly\n- Avoid sudden movements\n- Keep cameras ready — time is limited\n\nExplore all Thailand Packages here!\n\n### Location, Tickets & Transfers\n### \n📍 **Tiger Kingdom Phuket**, Kathu\n\n- Around 15–20 minutes from Patong Beach\n\n **Tiger Kingdom Phuket Ticket Price Packages** vary based on:\n\n- Number of tiger zones\n- Type of tigers selected\n- Photography add-ons\n\n **Transfers Available:**\n\n- **Tiger Kingdom with transfer from Patong, Karon & Kata**\n- Easy to combine with Big Buddha or Phuket City tour\n\n\n### Safety Rules & Family Guidelines\n### \n✔️ Always follow handler instructions\n\n✔️ No flash photography\n\n✔️ No sudden movements or loud noises\n\n✔️ Children allowed only in specific zones\n\n✔️ Closed shoes recommended\n\nMany families search **Tiger Kingdom family photos safety rules**, and the experience is designed to be controlled and supervised at all times.\n\nMajestic Thailand with Our Itinerary!\n\n### Ethical Notes – What You Should Know\n### \nTiger Kingdom often raises questions about animal ethics.\n\n**Important Points to Consider**\n\n- Tigers are **captive-bred**, not rescued\n- Interactions are structured and time-limited\n- Handlers closely monitor tiger behaviour\n- Not a sanctuary — it is an **interaction-based attraction**\n\nIf you prefer observation-only experiences, consider **ethical elephant sanctuaries** instead. Travellers often compare **Tiger Kingdom ethical concerns Phuket vs Chiang Mai**, and expectations should be set clearly before visiting.\n\n\n### Best Time to Visit Tiger Kingdom Phuket\n### \n✔️ Morning (cooler, active tigers)\n\n✔️ Weekdays for fewer crowds\n\n✔️ Avoid late afternoons during peak season\n\nAverage visit duration: **2–3 hours**\n\n\n### Combine Tiger Kingdom with Nearby Attractions\n### \nPopular combinations include:\n\n- Tiger Kingdom + **Big Buddha Phuket**\n- Tiger Kingdom + **Patong Beach**\n- Tiger Kingdom + **Phuket Old Town**\n- Tiger Kingdom + **Hanuman World Zipline**\n\n\n### Book Tiger Kingdom Phuket with India Tour Expeditions\n### \nAt **India Tour Expeditions**, we help Indian travellers choose wildlife experiences that match their comfort and expectations.\n\n✔️ Tiger Kingdom Phuket tickets & packages\n\n✔️ Hotel transfers from Patong, Kata & Karon\n\n✔️ Family-friendly planning\n\n✔️ Phuket sightseeing combos\n\n🐯 Add **Tiger Kingdom** to your Phuket itinerary for a bold and memorable wildlife encounter.",
