        "id": 848,
        "name": "Koh Panyee",
        "brief": "Floating Fishing Village",
        "description": "**Koh Panyee Floating Village**, also known as **Ko Panyi Phang Nga Bay**, is a unique village built entirely on wooden stilts over the sea. Located in the heart of Phang Nga Bay, Koh Panyee Thailand is home to a close-knit Muslim fishing community that has lived here for over 200 years.\n\nSurrounded by dramatic limestone cliffs, Koh Panyee Muslim village Thailand is one of the most fascinating cultural stops on Phang Nga Bay and James Bond Island tours. The village is famous for its colourful houses, narrow wooden walkways, waterfront seafood restaurants, mosque, and the iconic Koh Panyee floating football pitch.\n\nThis guide covers everything you need to know about visiting Koh Panyee, including its history, what to see, how to reach, cultural etiquette, and how it fits into popular island tours.\n\n\n### Why Visit Koh Panyee on Phang Nga Bay Tours\n### \n- One of Thailand’s most unique **floating villages**\n- Authentic **Muslim community in Phang Nga Bay**\n- Famous **floating football field Panyee FC**\n- Great stop on **James Bond Island and Koh Panyee day trip**\n- Excellent seafood lunch options\n- Insight into traditional fishing village life\n\nFor Indian travellers, Koh Panyee offers a rare cultural experience beyond beaches and viewpoints.\n\n\n### Koh Panyee Location & Background\n### \n📍 Located in **Phang Nga Bay**, southern Thailand\n- Built on stilts at the base of a limestone cliff\n- Accessible only by boat\n\nThe village has no natural land area—homes, schools, shops, and walkways are all constructed over the water.\n\n\n### History and Life in the Stilt Village\n### \nKoh Panyee has a fascinating origin story.\n\n### Bugis Fishermen Origins and Floating Football Pitch\n### \nKey historical highlights:\n\n- Founded by **Bugis fishermen from Java** over 200 years ago\n- Settled under limestone cliffs to avoid storms\n- Developed into a permanent fishing village\n- Created the world-famous **Koh Panyee football pitch** built on floating platforms\n\nThe floating football field became internationally famous after local children built it from scrap materials and later formed a successful youth team.\n\n\n### What to See at Koh Panyee Floating Village\n### \nA visit to Koh Panyee is short but memorable.\n\n#### Walkways, Mosque, Seafood and Shops\n#### \nThings to explore in the village:\n\n- **Wooden walkways and colourful stilt houses**\n- Local **mosque of the Koh Panyee Muslim community**\n- Waterfront **Koh Panyee seafood restaurants**\n- Souvenir stalls selling handicrafts\n- Views of limestone cliffs rising behind the village\n\nSeafood lunches here are commonly included in tour packages.\n\n\n### Best Time to Visit Koh Panyee\n### \n**Best Season:**\n\n✔️ November to April (dry season)\n\n**Best Time of Day:**\n\n✔️ Late morning to early afternoon (with lunch stop)\n\n Most travellers visit Koh Panyee as part of a full-day Phang Nga Bay tour.\n\n\n### How to Reach Koh Panyee\n### \nKoh Panyee is accessible only by boat.\n\n- Included in **Koh Panyee village tour from Phuket or Krabi**\n- Longtail or speedboat from **Phang Nga Pier**\n- Common stop on **James Bond Island tour**\n\nMany visitors search **how to reach Koh Panyee longtail boat Phang Nga Pier** when planning their trip.\n\n### Koh Panyee Dress Code & Cultural Etiquette\n### \nAs Koh Panyee is a Muslim village, respectful dressing is important.\n\n- Cover shoulders and knees\n- Avoid swimwear inside the village\n- Remove shoes when entering religious spaces\n- Be respectful while photographing locals\n\nFollowing the **Koh Panyee dress code Muslim village** guidelines ensures a positive experience.\n\n\n### Combine Koh Panyee with Nearby Attractions\n### \nKoh Panyee is usually combined with:\n\n- **James Bond Island (Khao Phing Kan)**\n- Sea cave canoeing in Phang Nga Bay\n- Mangrove forests and limestone lagoons\n\nThe **Koh Panyee James Bond Island tour** is one of the most popular day trips from Phuket.\n\n\n### Tips for Visiting Koh Panyee\n### \n- Carry small cash for souvenirs\n- Expect narrow walkways—wear comfortable shoes\n- Respect local customs and privacy\n- Lunch stops usually last **45–60 minutes**\n- Follow guide instructions during village visits\n\n\n### Explore Koh Panyee with India Tour Expeditions\n### \nAt **India Tour Expeditions**, we curate cultural and scenic Phang Nga Bay experiences for Indian travellers.\n\n✔️ **Koh Panyee floating village tours**\n\n✔️ James Bond Island & Phang Nga Bay itineraries\n\n✔️ Guided cultural experiences\n\n✔️ Thailand tour packages from India\n\n🌊 Add **Koh Panyee Floating Village** to your Thailand itinerary and discover one of Thailand’s most remarkable communities built entirely over water.",
