        "name": "Chicken Island (Koh Gai)",
        "brief": "Famous Rock-Shaped Island with Snorkelling & Clear Blue Waters",
        "description": "**Chicken Island**, also known as **Koh Gai** or **Koh Kai Chicken Island**, is one of the most iconic islands in Krabi and a highlight of the popular **4 Islands Tour**. Located close to Ao Nang, **Chicken Island Krabi** is best known for its unique chicken-head-shaped rock formation, clear shallow waters, and excellent snorkeling spots.\n\nPart of a protected marine area, **Chicken Island Thailand** is often visited alongside Poda Island and Tub Island. During low tide, a natural sandbar emerges, allowing visitors to walk between nearby islands—making it one of the most photographed island experiences in Krabi.\n\nThis guide covers everything you need to know about visiting **Koh Gai Ao Nang**, including snorkeling highlights, sandbar timings, how to reach, and essential travel tips.\n\n\n### Why Visit Chicken Island Near Ao Nang\n### \n- Famous **chicken head rock formation in Krabi**\n- Excellent **Chicken Island snorkeling reefs**\n- Unique **low tide sandbar at Chicken Island**\n- Shallow waters ideal for swimming\n- Part of the classic **Chicken Island Four Islands Tour**\n- Easy access from Ao Nang by boat\n\nFor Indian travellers, Chicken Island offers a perfect mix of sightseeing, swimming, and snorkeling in a short island visit.\n\n\n### Chicken Island Location & Background\n### \n📍 Located off the coast of **Ao Nang, Krabi**\n- Officially known as **Koh Gai / Koh Kai**\n- Part of a protected marine national park area\n\nThe island gets its name from a limestone rock that resembles a chicken’s head and neck, visible clearly from the sea.\n\n\n### Highlights and Snorkeling Spots\n### \nChicken Island is particularly popular for its underwater life and clear waters.\n\n#### Chicken Head Rock and Low-Tide Sandbar\n#### \nKey highlights include:\n\n- The iconic **chicken head rock formation**\n- Coral reefs close to shore\n- **Shallow waters at Koh Gai** ideal for beginner swimmers\n- Colourful reef fish and marine life\n- A natural sandbar that appears during low tide\n\n🌊 The **best time to see the Chicken Island sandbar at low tide** is usually mid-day, depending on tide conditions.\n\nPlan your Thailand Vacation at Phuket and Krabi\n\n### How to Reach on 4 Islands Tour from Krabi\n### \n**From Ao Nang:**\n\n- Longtail boat or speedboat\n- Approx. **15–20 minutes**\n- Commonly included in **Chicken Island Krabi from Ao Nang longtail boat** routes\n\n**Tour Option:**\n\n- **4 Islands Tour (Chicken Island, Poda Island, Tub Island, Phra Nang Cave)**\n- Also known as **4 Islands Tour Chicken Island Poda Tub Mor**\n\nMost travellers visit Chicken Island as part of a guided tour rather than independently.\n\n\n### Best Time to Visit Chicken Island\n### \n**Best Season:**\n\n✔️ November to April (dry season, calm sea)\n\n**Best Time for Sandbar & Snorkeling:**\n\n✔️ Mid-day during **low tide**\n\n✔️ Morning hours for clearer water visibility\n\nThe **best time to visit Chicken Island for snorkeling** is during the dry season with low waves.\n\n### Chicken Island National Park Fee\n### \n- Chicken Island falls under a **marine national park**\n- **Chicken Island national park fee** is applicable\n- Fee is usually collected during island tours\n- Helps support coral and marine conservation\n\n\n### Chicken Island vs Phi Phi Snorkeling\n### \nWhile Phi Phi Islands are larger and more dramatic, **Chicken Island snorkeling** is calmer, less crowded, and ideal for beginners. It is a better option for travellers looking for a short, relaxed snorkeling experience near Ao Nang.\n\n\n### Tips, Tides and Marine Life of Chicken Island\n### \n- Check tide timings for the sandbar experience\n- Wear water shoes for rocky areas\n- Use reef-safe sunscreen only\n- Do not touch coral or marine life\n- Follow guide instructions strictly\n\n\n### Explore Chicken Island with India Tour Expeditions\n### \nAt **India Tour Expeditions**, we curate island-hopping experiences for Indian travellers.\n\n✔️ **Chicken Island Krabi tours**\n\n✔️ **4 Islands Tour from Ao Nang**\n\n✔️ Snorkeling-friendly itineraries\n\n✔️ Seamless Thailand travel planning\n\n🏝️ Add **Chicken Island (Koh Gai)** to your Krabi itinerary and experience one of the region’s most unique island landmarks.",
