        "id": 410,
        "name": "Tup Island",
        "brief": "Unique Sandbar Island Connecting Two Islands at Low Tide",
        "description": "**Tup Island Krabi**,also known as Koh Tup Talay Waek, is one of the most iconic natural attractions in Thailand, famous for the spectacular Talay Waek divided sea phenomenon. During low tide, a pristine white-sand sandbar emerges, connecting Tup Island, Chicken Island, and Mor Island, allowing visitors to walk across the sea itself.\n\nLocated just off the coast of Ao Nang, Tup Island is a highlight of the popular Tup Island Four Islands Tour and a must-visit for travellers exploring Krabi. The island is part of a protected national park and is known for its shallow turquoise waters, coral sand, and postcard-perfect scenery.\n\nThis guide covers everything you need to know about visiting **Tup Island Krabi**, including the Talay Waek phenomenon, snorkeling experience, tour options from Ao Nang and Railay, national park fees, low-tide timing, and the best season to visit.\n\n\n### Why Visit Tup Island Krabi\n### \n- Witness the famous **Talay Waek Krabi divided sea**\n- Walk across a natural **low-tide sandbar**\n- Shallow turquoise water with white coral sand\n- One of the most scenic stops on the **Four Islands Tour**\n- Short and easy visit suitable for families\n- Ideal for photography and first-time visitors to Krabi\n\nFor Indian travellers looking for a **unique natural experience without long travel**, Tup Island offers a rare and memorable highlight.\n\n\n### Tup Island Location & Background\n### \n📍 **Tup Island Krabi**, Andaman Sea\n- Part of the **Hat Noppharat Thara–Mu Ko Phi Phi National Park**\n- Located between **Chicken Island and Mor Island**\n- Accessible only by boat from Ao Nang or Railay\n\nThe island is small, undeveloped, and protected, with **no permanent structures or facilities**, preserving its natural charm.\n\n\n### Best Time to Visit Tup Island & Talay Waek\n### \n**Best Season:**\n\n✔️ **November to April** – calm seas and clear visibility\n\n**Best Time of Day:**\n\n✔️ **Low tide**, when the Talay Waek sandbar appears\n\nMany travellers search for the **Tup Island Krabi low tide timing chart**, as sandbar visibility depends entirely on daily tide conditions. Morning tours usually offer the best chance to see the sandbar fully exposed. At high tide, the sandbar disappears completely.\n\n\n### Beach & Snorkeling Experience at Tup Island\n### \nSnorkeling and shallow swimming are popular around Tup Island.\n\nWhat you can expect:\n\n- Clear water with good visibility on calm days\n- Sightings of **colorful fish and sea urchins**\n- Small coral patches near rocky edges\n- Shallow depth ideal for beginners\n\n**Reef shoes are strongly recommended** due to coral sand and sea urchins.\n\nThere are **no shops, restrooms, or shade**, so visitors should carry water, sunscreen, and hats.\n\n\n### Chicken Island, Mor Island & Photo Opportunities\n### \nOne of the biggest highlights of Tup Island is its proximity to nearby islands.\n\n- **Chicken Island** – famous for its chicken-head rock formation\n- **Mor Island** – smaller and quieter, visible during low tide\n- Open sea views and limestone cliffs in every direction\n\nThe **Talay Waek sandbar walking path** is one of the most photographed spots in Krabi, especially when the sand curves naturally between the islands.\n\n\n### Four Islands Tours from Ao Nang, NP Fee & Tide Timings\n### \n**How to Visit Tup Island:**\n\nTup Island is included in:\n\n- **Four Islands Tour Ao Nang**\n- Longtail boat tours\n- Speedboat island-hopping tours\n\nTypical Four Islands Tour covers:\n\n- Tup Island (Talay Waek)\n- Chicken Island\n- **Poda Island**\n- **Phra Nang Beach**\n\n**National Park Fee:**\n\n**200 THB per adult**\n\n(collected separately on the islands)\n\nTour operators plan routes around tides, but exact sandbar conditions depend on nature.\n\n\n### Combine Tup Island with Nearby Attractions\n### \nPopular combinations include:\n\n- **Tup Island + Chicken Island + Poda Island**\n- Tup Island + **Phra Nang Beach**\n- Railay Beach island-hopping tour\n\nThis makes Tup Island ideal for a **half-day island tour from Ao Nang, Railay, or Krabi Town**.\n\n\n### Book Tup Island Tour with India Tour Expeditions\n### \nAt **India Tour Expeditions**, we design Krabi island experiences specially for Indian travellers.\n\n✔️ **Four Islands Tour from Ao Nang**\n\n✔️ Guided island-hopping itineraries\n\n✔️ Transparent pricing with national park fee guidance\n\n✔️ Easy add-on with Railay & Phra Nang Beach\n\n🌊 Add **Tup Island** to your Krabi itinerary and experience Thailand’s most famous divided sea phenomenon.",
