        "description": "**Ko Poda Island Krabi**, also known as **Koh Poda Island Thailand**, is one of the most beautiful small islands located just off the coast of **Ao Nang**. Famous for its powdery white sand, crystal-clear turquoise water, and a dramatic limestone rock rising offshore, **Poda Island Krabi** is a highlight of most island-hopping itineraries.\n\nPart of the **Hat Noppharat Thara–Mu Ko Phi Phi National Park**, **Ko Poda Beach Ao Nang** offers a postcard-perfect tropical escape. The island is commonly visited on the popular **Poda Island 4 Islands Tour**, making it an easy and rewarding half-day trip from Ao Nang or Railay Beach.\n\nThis guide covers everything you need to know about visiting **Ko Poda Island**, including why it’s famous, beach and snorkeling highlights, how to reach, national park fees, best time to visit, and useful travel tips.\n\nPlan your family vacation with Best of Thailand Itinerary!\n\n### Why Visit Poda Island off Ao Nang\n### \n- One of the most scenic islands near Ao Nang\n- Stunning **white sand beach Poda Island**\n- Calm, **crystal clear turquoise water**\n- Iconic limestone rock formation offshore\n- Great snorkeling and swimming conditions\n- Easy stop on Krabi island-hopping tours\n\nFor Indian travellers, Poda Island is ideal for relaxing beach time combined with light snorkeling.\n\n\n### Ko Poda Island Location & Background\n### \n📍 Located off the coast of **Ao Nang, Krabi**\n- Part of **Mu Ko Phi Phi National Park**\n- Accessible only by boat\n\nThe island remains largely undeveloped, preserving its natural charm.\n\n\n## Beach, Snorkeling and Iconic Rock Scenery\n\nKo Poda Island is best known for its scenic simplicity. What you’ll experience on the island:\n\n- Long stretch of **white sand beach**\n- Clear, shallow water near the shore\n- **Snorkeling reefs around Koh Poda**\n- Famous **limestone rock in front of Poda Island**\n- Quieter beach areas away from boat drop-off points\n\nWalking further along the beach helps escape crowds and enjoy peaceful spots.\n\n\n### Best Time to Visit Ko Poda Island\n### \n**Best Season:**\n\n✔️ **November to April** (dry season)\n\n**Best Time of Day:**\n\n✔️ Early morning for fewer crowds\n\n✔️ Late afternoon for softer light\n\nMany travellers look for **best time to visit Poda Island November to April** for calm seas and clear visibility.\n\n\n### How to Reach Poda Island\n### \nKo Poda Island is accessible only by boat.\n\n- Included in **Krabi 4 Islands Tour including Poda Island**\n- Longtail boats from **Ao Nang or Railay**\n- Speedboat island-hopping packages\n\nThe **Poda Island day trip from Ao Nang or Railay** usually takes 4–6 hours including other islands.\n\n\n### Ko Poda Island National Park Entrance Fee\n### \n**Entrance Fee:**\n\n✔️ Approx. **300 Baht per adult**\n\nPaid to **Hat Noppharat Thara–Mu Ko Phi Phi National Park**\n\nFees support conservation and island maintenance.\n\n\n### Poda Island vs Chicken and Tub Island Krabi\n### \n- **Poda Island**: Best beach and scenic views\n- **Chicken Island**: Unique rock shape and snorkeling\n- **Tub Island**: Famous sandbar at low tide\n\nAll three are commonly visited together on the **4 Islands Tour**.\n\n### Tips for Visiting Ko Poda Island\n### \n- Carry cash for park fees\n- Bring reef-safe sunscreen\n- Wear water shoes for rocky snorkeling areas\n- Walk away from boat zones for quieter beaches\n- Allocate **45–60 minutes** on the island\n\n### Explore Ko Poda Island with India Tour Expeditions\n### \nAt **India Tour Expeditions**, we curate seamless Krabi island experiences for Indian travellers.\n\n✔️ **Ko Poda Island tours from Ao Nang**\n\n✔️ 4 Islands island-hopping packages\n\n✔️ Snorkeling-focused itineraries\n\n✔️ Thailand tour packages from India\n\n🏖️ Add **Ko Poda Island Krabi (Koh Poda)** to your Thailand itinerary and enjoy one of Krabi’s most photogenic tropical islands.",
