        "brief": "Small Island Nestled in Phang Nga Bay",
        "description": "**Koh Khai Nok**, also known as **Khai Nok Island Phuket**, is one of the most popular small islands located just off the east coast of Phuket. Part of the famous **Khai Islands Phuket tour**, this tiny island is known for its soft white sand, shallow turquoise waters, and colourful fish that swim right up to the shoreline.\n\nA **Koh Khai Nok day trip from Phuket** is perfect for families, first-time snorkellers, and travellers looking for a relaxed island experience without long boat rides. The island is compact, easy to explore, and offers basic facilities such as beach chairs, snack bars, and shaded seating.\n\nThis guide covers everything you need to know about visiting **Koh Khai Nok Island**, including snorkeling highlights, facilities, tour options, best time to visit, and how it compares to other nearby islands.\n\n\n### Why Visit Koh Khai Nok from Phuket\n### \n- One of the easiest island escapes near Phuket\n- Beautiful **white sand beach Koh Khai Nok**\n- Calm, shallow water with fish near the shore\n- Ideal for **family friendly snorkelling near Phuket**\n- Well-managed island with basic facilities\n- Perfect half-day trip option\n\nFor Indian travellers, Koh Khai Nok offers an easy and enjoyable introduction to island hopping in Thailand.\n\n\n### Koh Khai Nok Location & Background\n### \n 📍 Located off Phuket’s east coast\n- Part of the **Khai Island group**\n- Accessible only by boat\n\nThe island is small and privately managed, helping maintain facilities and cleanliness.\n\n\n### Beach, Snorkelling and Facilities on Khai Nok\n### \nKoh Khai Nok is all about easy beach enjoyment.\n\n\n#### Fish-Filled Shallows, Sunbeds, Bars and Water Sports\n#### \nWhat you’ll experience on the island:\n\n- **Shallow turquoise water with fish** right at the beach\n- Easy **Koh Khai Nok snorkeling** for beginners\n- Sunbeds and umbrellas for rent\n- Small beach bars serving drinks and snacks\n- Optional water sports like kayaking\n\nThe fish are accustomed to visitors and often gather close to the shoreline.\n\n\n### Khai Island Group – Khai Nai, Khai Nok and Khai Nui Overview\n### \nThe Khai Islands usually come as a group tour.\n\n- **Khai Nok** – best facilities and snorkeling near shore\n- **Khai Nai** – similar beach experience with more space\n- **Khai Nui** – deeper water snorkeling and coral\n\nMost visitors choose the **3 Khai Islands tour Khai Nai Khai Nok Khai Nui**.\n\n\n### Best Time to Visit Koh Khai Nok Island\n### \n**Best Season:**\n\n✔️ November to April (dry season)\n\n**Best Time of Day:**\n\n✔️ Morning hours for calm seas and fewer crowds\n\nMany travellers look for **best time to visit Koh Khai Nok morning calm sea** for clearer water and relaxed beach time.\n\n\n### How to Reach Koh Khai Nok & Tour Options\n### \n- Speedboat from Phuket (15–30 minutes)\n- Included in **Koh Khai Nok half day tour from Phuket**\n- Transfers usually included from hotels\n\nTours operate daily, weather permitting.\n\n\n### Koh Khai Nok National Park Fee\n### \n- Some tours include island access fees\n- Others may charge a small **Koh Khai Nok national park fee** separately\n\nAlways confirm what’s included in your tour package.\n\n\n### Koh Khai Nok vs Coral Island for Snorkelling\n### \n- **Koh Khai Nok**: Shallow water, beginner-friendly snorkeling\n- **Coral Island**: More water sports and larger beaches\n\nKoh Khai Nok is better for families and first-time snorkellers.\n\n\n### Tips for Visiting Koh Khai Nok\n### \n- Bring reef-safe sunscreen\n- Carry cash for sunbeds or drinks\n- Avoid feeding fish excessively\n- Wear water shoes if needed\n- Allocate **1–1.5 hours** on the island\n\n\n### Explore Koh Khai Nok with India Tour Expeditions\n### \nAt **India Tour Expeditions**, we curate easy island escapes for Indian travellers.\n\n✔️ **Koh Khai Nok day trips from Phuket**\n\n✔️ Khai Islands speedboat tours\n\n✔️ Family-friendly island itineraries\n\n✔️ Thailand tour packages from India\n\n🏝️ Add **Koh Khai Nok Island Phuket** to your Thailand itinerary and enjoy a relaxed, fish-filled island escape close to Phuket.",
