        "id": 430,
        "name": "Tiger Cave Temple",
        "brief": "Sacred Hilltop Temple with 1,237 Steps",
        "description": "The **Tiger Cave Temple Krabi**, locally known as **Wat Tham Sua**, is one of the most iconic spiritual and adventure attractions in southern Thailand. Famous for its **1,237 steep steps** leading to a dramatic hilltop summit, the temple rewards climbers with breathtaking **360° views over Krabi’s limestone cliffs, jungle valleys, and farmlands**.\n\nAt the top sits a majestic **golden Buddha statue**, making the climb both a physical challenge and a spiritual journey. Whether you’re visiting for faith, fitness, photography, or personal achievement, **Tiger Cave Temple Thailand** is a must-do experience for travellers exploring Krabi beyond beaches and islands.\n\nThis guide covers the climb, caves, legends, timings, how to reach from Ao Nang or Krabi Town, and practical tips for first-time visitors.\n\n\n### Why Climb Tiger Cave Temple Krabi\n### \n- One of Krabi’s **most famous viewpoints**\n- Legendary **1,237-step climb** (bucket-list challenge)\n- Panoramic views from **Wat Tham Sua viewpoint**\n- Sacred caves, meditation areas & monk residences\n- Free entry and deeply spiritual atmosphere\n- A rewarding alternative to beach sightseeing\n\nFor Indian travellers, the temple offers a powerful mix of **devotion, discipline, and natural beauty**.\n\n\n### The Legend Behind Tiger Cave Temple\n### \nThe name **Wat Tham Sua** comes from a local legend that tigers once lived in the caves of this limestone hill. Inside the temple complex, you’ll find:\n\n- **Tiger paw prints** embedded in stone\n-  Ancient **meditation caves**\n-  Shrines and Buddha images at ground level\n\nThe site is still an active monastery, and monks continue to live and meditate here.\n\n### The 1,237 Steps, Golden Buddha & Views\n### \n#### What to Expect During the Climb\n#### \n- ✔️ **1,237 steep concrete steps**\n- ✔️ Handrails on most sections\n- ✔️ Narrow and uneven stair segments\n- ✔️ Increasingly spectacular views as you climb\n\nAt the summit:\n\n- A large **golden Buddha statue**\n-  Sacred **Buddha footprint**\n- Uninterrupted views of **Krabi’s jungle valley, cliffs & countryside**\n\nMost visitors take **30–60 minutes to climb up** and **20–30 minutes to descend**, depending on fitness.\n\nCombine Phuket and Krabi in one Thailand trip!\n\n### Tiger Paw Prints, Meditation Caves & Photo Spots\n### \nBefore or after the climb, explore the lower temple complex:\n\n-  **Tiger paw print cave**\n-  Meditation caves carved into limestone\n-  **Kiriwong Valley** jungle views\n-  Calm photo spots without crowds\n\nThese areas are less strenuous and suitable for visitors who don’t wish to climb.\n\n### Location, Entry, Opening Hours & Transport\n### \n📍 **Tiger Cave Temple Krabi**, near Krabi Town\n\n **Entry Fee:**\n\n Free (donations welcome)\n\n **Opening Hours:**\n\n✔️ Early morning to evening (best to start early)\n\n **How to Reach:**\n\n- From **Krabi Town:** 15–20 minutes by taxi\n- From **Ao Nang:** 30–40 minutes by taxi or Grab\n\nMany travellers search **how to reach Wat Tham Sua from Ao Nang or Krabi Town**, and taxis are the most convenient option.\n\nExplore Thailand Tour Packages here!\n\n### Best Time to Visit Tiger Cave Temple\n### \n✔️ **Best time of day:** Early morning (cooler, fewer crowds)\n\n✔️ **Best season:** November to February\n\n✔️ **Avoid:** Midday heat & slippery steps after rain\n\nThose looking for **best time Tiger Cave Temple morning cooler less crowds** should aim to arrive before 8 AM.\n\n\n### Tips for Hikers & First-Time Visitors\n### \n- Carry **plenty of water**\n- Wear proper walking shoes (no slippers)\n- Take breaks — no rush\n- Watch out for **monkeys**\n- Hold railings while descending\n- Skip the climb if you have knee or heart issues\n\nThe climb is **physically demanding** and not suitable for everyone.\n\n\n### Tiger Cave Temple vs Railay Viewpoints\n### \n- **Tiger Cave Temple:** Harder climb, higher reward, spiritual setting\n- **Railay viewpoints:** Shorter but slippery, more adventure-focused\n\nChoose Tiger Cave Temple if you want a **challenge with cultural meaning**.\n\n\n### Combine Tiger Cave Temple with Other Krabi Experiences\n### \nPopular combinations include:\n\n- Tiger Cave Temple + **Krabi Town Night Market**\n- Tiger Cave Temple + **Emerald Pool & Hot Springs**\n- Tiger Cave Temple + **Krabi City temples**\n\n### Visit Tiger Cave Temple with India Tour Expeditions\n### \nAt **India Tour Expeditions**, we help Indian travellers experience Krabi beyond beaches.\n\n✔️ Tiger Cave Temple visits\n\n✔️ Krabi cultural sightseeing\n\n✔️ Private transfers from Ao Nang & Krabi Town\n\n✔️ Custom Krabi itineraries\n\nAdd **Wat Tham Sua Krabi** to your Thaialnd trip for a powerful mix of faith, fitness, and unforgettable views.",
