        "id": 906,
        "name": "Underwater World",
        "brief": "Thailand’s First Walk-Through Underwater Tunnel Aquarium",
        "description": "**Aquaria Phuket** is Thailand’s largest and most modern aquarium, located inside **Central Phuket Floresta**. Often searched as the successor to **Underwater World Pattaya (now closed)**, Aquaria offers a world-class indoor marine experience featuring a 100-metre underwater tunnel, thousands of marine creatures, and interactive family-friendly zones.\n\nSpanning multiple themed ecosystems, **Aquaria Phuket Thailand** is a perfect attraction for families, couples, and travellers looking for **indoor things to do in Phuket**, especially during hot afternoons or rainy days. Highlights include sharks, stingrays, penguins, otters, mermaid underwater ballet shows, and hands-on touch pools.\n\nThis guide covers everything you need to know about **Aquaria Phuket tickets**, opening hours, zones, shows, how it compares to Pattaya’s Underwater World, and tips for planning your visit.\n\n\n### Why Visit Aquaria Phuket Thailand\n### \n- **Thailand’s largest aquarium**\n- Modern replacement for **Underwater World Pattaya (closed)**\n- Massive **underwater tunnel with sharks and rays**\n- Popular **Aquaria Phuket mermaid show**\n- Interactive touch pools for kids\n- Fully air-conditioned, indoor attraction\n- Easy to combine with shopping and dining\n\nFor Indian travellers visiting Phuket with family, **Aquaria Phuket** is one of the most convenient and enjoyable attractions in the city.\n\n\n### Aquaria Zones – Mystic Forest, Sharks, Mermaids and Otters\n### \nAquaria is divided into immersive zones representing different aquatic ecosystems.\n\nMain zones include:\n\n- **Mystic Forest** – freshwater species, reptiles, and jungle habitats\n- **Coastal Haven** – coral reefs, colourful fish, and shallow-water species\n- **South China Sea** – sharks, giant stingrays, and pelagic fish\n- **Penguin & Otter Zone** – one of the most loved sections for kids\n\nEach zone is designed with educational displays and clear viewing panels, making it engaging for all age groups.\n\n\n### Highlights – Underwater Tunnel, Shows, Touch Pools and Dining\n### \nOne of the biggest attractions at Aquaria is the **100-metre underwater tunnel**, where visitors walk beneath sharks, rays, and schooling fish.\n\n**What to Expect Inside**\n\n- Shark tunnel with panoramic views\n- **Mermaid underwater ballet performances**\n- Scheduled **feeding sessions**\n- Touch pools with **starfish and horseshoe crabs**\n- Interactive learning displays for children\n- Café and dining options within Central Phuket Floresta\n\nThe **best time to watch the Aquaria Phuket mermaid show** is mid-day to early afternoon, depending on the daily schedule.\n\n\n### Feeding Sessions, Mermaid Ballet and Family Activities\n### \nDaily activities make Aquaria more than just a walk-through aquarium.\n\nPopular experiences include:\n\n- Shark and stingray feeding sessions\n- Otter and penguin feeding times\n- Mermaid underwater ballet (timing varies by day)\n- Educational talks for children\n\nFamilies planning their visit often check the **Aquaria Phuket mermaid show schedule** and feeding timings in advance to plan breaks.\n\n\n### Location in Central Phuket, Hours, Tickets and Patong Transfers\n### \n📍 **Location:**\n\nAquaria Phuket is located inside **Central Phuket Floresta**, making it easy to combine with shopping and meals.\n\n **Opening Hours:**\n\nTypically **10:30 AM – 7:00 PM**\n\n(Last entry around 6:00 PM)\n\n **Tickets:**\n\nTicket prices vary by season and combo options.\n\nCommon options include:\n\n- Standard aquarium ticket\n- **Aquaria Phuket family ticket**\n- **Aquaria Phuket + Trick Eye Museum combo**\n\nTransfers from **Patong, Karon, and Kata** are easily available by taxi or pre-booked transport.\n\n\n### Aquaria Phuket vs Underwater World Pattaya\n### \n**Underwater World Pattaya** has permanently closed, and **Aquaria Phuket** is now considered Thailand’s most advanced aquarium experience.\n\n**Key Differences**\n\n- Aquaria is larger, newer, and more interactive\n- Features mermaid shows and modern themed zones\n- Located inside a premium mall with dining options\n- Better suited for families and full-day city plans\n\nIf you’ve visited Underwater World Pattaya earlier, **Aquaria Phuket is a clear upgrade** in scale and experience.\n\n\n### Best Time to Visit Aquaria Phuket & Tips\n### \n**Best Time of Day:**\n\n✔️ Late morning or early afternoon\n\n✔️ Ideal during hot weather or rain\n\n**Helpful Tips:**\n\n- Allow **1.5 to 2 hours** for the visit\n- Combine with lunch or shopping at Central Phuket\n- Check feeding & mermaid show timings on arrival\n- Comfortable footwear recommended\n\n\n### Book Aquaria Phuket with India Tour Expeditions\n### \nAt **India Tour Expeditions**, we help Indian travellers plan Phuket itineraries that balance sightseeing, relaxation, and family-friendly attractions.\n\n✔️ **Aquaria Phuket tickets & combos**\n\n✔️ Easy transfers from Patong & city hotels\n\n✔️ Family-friendly Phuket tour planning\n\n✔️ Add-on with Old Town, Big Buddha & shows\n\n🌊 Add **Aquaria Phuket** to your Phuket trip and enjoy a world-class underwater experience.",
