        "id": 838,
        "name": "Lamai Beach",
        "brief": "Second-Largest and Second Most Popular Beach",
        "description": "**Lamai Beach** is one of the most popular and scenic beaches in **Koh Samui**, offering the perfect balance between relaxation and entertainment for Indian travellers. Known for its long stretch of soft sand, clear blue waters, and laid-back atmosphere, Lamai Beach is ideal for those who want a peaceful beach holiday without being completely cut off from nightlife, restaurants, and shopping.\n\nUnlike the more crowded Chaweng Beach, **Lamai Beach Koh Samui** feels calmer, more spacious, and slightly more local—making it a favourite among Indian families, honeymooners, couples, and long-stay travellers. With beachside resorts, Indian-friendly food options, massage centres, and easy access to nearby attractions, Lamai is a well-rounded destination in Koh Samui.\n\nThis complete guide helps you plan your visit to **Lamai Beach**, covering the **best time to visit, things to do, nightlife, hotels, and how to reach**, ensuring a smooth and memorable island experience.\n\n\n### Why Lamai Beach Is a Must-Visit in Koh Samui\n\n- One of the **best beaches in Koh Samui for Indian travellers**\n- Cleaner, quieter, and less crowded than Chaweng\n- Ideal for **families, couples, and honeymooners**\n- Good mix of beach relaxation and nightlife\n- Easy access to temples, viewpoints, and local markets\n- Stunning sunsets and scenic coastal views\n\nCompared to other Koh Samui beaches, **Lamai Beach** offers a more relaxed yet lively experience.\n\n\n### Best Time to Visit Lamai Beach\n\nThe best time to visit **Lamai Beach Koh Samui** is:\n\n- **December to April:** Dry season, sunny weather, calm sea\n- **May to September:** Warm weather with occasional showers\n- **October to November:** Higher rainfall, fewer tourists\n\n🕗 **Best Time of Day:**\n\n- Morning for swimming and beach walks\n- Evening for **sunset views and beachside dining**\n\n\n### Things to Do at Lamai Beach\n\nLamai Beach offers a wide range of activities suitable for Indian travellers of all age groups.\n\n✔️ Swimming & sunbathing\n\n✔️ Beach massages & Thai spa treatments\n\n✔️ Jet skiing & water sports\n\n✔️ Beachside cafés and sunset dining\n\n✔️ Exploring nearby attractions like **Hin Ta Hin Yai (Grandfather & Grandmother Rocks)**\n\n✔️ Shopping at Lamai Night Market\n\nThis makes Lamai Beach ideal for **both relaxation and light adventure**.\n\n\n### Lamai Beach Nightlife & Dining\n\nThe **Lamai Beach nightlife** is lively but not overwhelming.\n\n- Beach bars with live music\n- Relaxed pubs and cocktail lounges\n- Fire shows on select nights\n- Night markets with street food & souvenirs\n\nIndian travellers will find **vegetarian-friendly options**, international cuisine, and some Indian restaurants around Lamai.\n\n\n### Best Hotels & Resorts in Lamai Beach\n\nLamai Beach offers accommodation options for every budget:\n\n- **Luxury beach resorts** with sea views\n- Mid-range hotels near the beach\n- Budget-friendly guesthouses\n- Family-friendly resorts with pools\n\nIndian travellers often prefer **beachfront resorts in Lamai** for comfort, views, and easy access to restaurants.\n\n\n### How to Reach Lamai Beach\n\n📍 Location: East coast of Koh Samui\n\n**How to Reach:**\n\n- Taxi or private cab from Koh Samui Airport (approx. 30 minutes)\n- Hotel transfers\n- Scooter or car rental\n\nLamai Beach is well connected and easy to reach from all parts of the island.\n\n\n### What to Expect at Lamai Beach\n\n- Clean, wide sandy beach with fewer crowds\n- Calm waters suitable for swimming\n- Friendly, relaxed beach vibe\n- Mix of locals, international tourists, and families\n- Affordable food and massage options\n\nThis is not a party-heavy destination, but a **balanced beach experience**.\n\n\n### What to Wear & Carry at Lamai Beach\n\n- Light beachwear & swimwear\n- Sunscreen & sunglasses\n- Flip-flops or sandals\n- Hat or cap\n- Cash for small shops and markets\n\n\n### Combine Lamai Beach with Koh Samui Experiences\n\nPopular combinations for Indian travellers:\n\n- Lamai Beach + Chaweng sightseeing\n- Lamai + Big Buddha Temple\n- Lamai + island hopping tour\n- Lamai Beach + Ang Thong Marine Park day trip\n\n\n### Visit Lamai Beach with India Tour Expeditions\n\nAt **India Tour Expeditions**, we curate Koh Samui and Thailand itineraries designed especially for Indian travellers.\n\n✔️ **Koh Samui packages with Lamai Beach stay**\n\n✔️ Handpicked resorts & hotels\n\n✔️ Private transfers & sightseeing\n\n✔️ Custom Thailand itineraries from India\n\n🌴 Add **Lamai Beach, Koh Samui** to your Thailand itinerary and enjoy a relaxed tropical escape with comfort and convenience.",
