        "name": "Phra Nang Beach",
        "brief": "One of the Nicest Beaches on Railay Peninsula",
        "description": "**Phra Nang Beach Krabi** is one of the most beautiful and photographed beaches in Thailand, famous for its dramatic limestone cliffs, clear turquoise water, and the sacred **Princess Cave (Phra Nang Cave)** at one end of the beach. Located on the Railay peninsula, this beach is often referred to as **Railay Phra Nang Cave Beach**.\n\nAccessible only by boat, **Phra Nang Beach Thailand** offers a perfect mix of natural beauty, calm swimming conditions, spiritual culture, and adventure activities like kayaking and rock climbing. For Indian travellers visiting Krabi, Phra Nang is a must-visit beach, whether as a short stop or a relaxed half-day outing.\n\nThis guide covers how to reach Phra Nang Beach from Ao Nang, best time to visit, swimming conditions for families, cave highlights, and activity tips.\n\n\n### Why Visit Phra Nang Beach in Krabi\n### \n- One of Thailand’s **most scenic limestone beaches**\n- Famous **Princess Cave Railay** spiritual site\n- Clear, shallow water suitable for swimming\n- Iconic views and photography spots\n- Popular stop on Railay and island-hopping tours\n- Combines beach time with culture and adventure\n\nPhra Nang Beach consistently ranks among the **top beaches in Krabi**.\n\nTropical Thailand Itinerary by India Tour Expeditions\n\n### What Phra Nang Beach Is Like (Sand, Sea and Scenery)\n### \n- Soft white sand with limestone cliffs on all sides\n- Calm, shallow water near the shore\n- Small rocky areas and caves at the edges\n- Less commercial than Ao Nang\n- Stunning backdrops for photos\n\nThe beach is especially popular for **sunset photography** and cliff-framed shots.\n\nPlan your vacation to Thailand now!\n\n### Princess Cave (Phra Nang Cave) – Spiritual Landmark\n### \nAt the southern end of the beach lies **Phra Nang Cave**, also known as the **Princess Cave Railay**.\n\n**What Makes the Cave Unique**\n\n- Sacred **lingam shrine** dedicated to the sea princess\n- Offerings from local fishermen\n- Cultural and spiritual significance\n- Short, easy walk from the beach\n\nVisitors should be respectful—this is an active place of worship.\n\n\n### Swimming, Kayaking and Family Experience\n### \n\n- ✔️ Best at **mid to high tide**\n- ✔️ Calm waters for families\n- ✔️ Sandy entry near the centre of the beach\n\nMany travellers look for a **Phra Nang Beach Railay family swimming guide**, and this beach is one of the safest in Railay.\n\n**Kayaking and Activities**\n\n- Kayak rentals available (seasonal)\n- Paddle along the cliffs and caves\n- Short-distance, beginner-friendly routes\n **Kayak rental Phra Nang Beach prices** vary by season and duration.\n\n\n### Rock Climbing at Phra Nang Beach\n### \nPhra Nang is also known for:\n\n- World-class **rock climbing routes**\n- Limestone cliff climbs for beginners and experts\n- Guided climbing tours from Railay\n\n The **Phra Nang Beach cliffs** are part of Krabi’s famous climbing scene.\n\n\n### How to Reach Phra Nang Beach\n### \n\n-  **Ao Nang to Phra Nang Beach longtail boat**\n- Travel time: ~15 minutes\n- Boats operate throughout the day\n\nMany visitors search **Phra Nang Beach boat from Ao Nang** when planning Krabi trips.\n\n**From Railay**\n\n- Short walk from Railay West via a marked trail\n- 10–15 minutes on foot\n\n📍 **Phra Nang Beach near Railay West**, making it easy to combine both beaches.\n\n\n### Best Time to Visit Phra Nang Beach\n### \n- ✔️ **November to April** – Best weather and water clarity\n- ✔️ Early morning – Fewer boats and softer light\n- ✔️ Late afternoon – Sunset views\n\n **Low tide** exposes rocks; **high tide** is better for swimming.\n\n\n### How Long to Spend at Phra Nang Beach\n### \n- 1–2 hours: Quick visit and photos\n- 3–4 hours: Swimming, cave visit and relaxation\n\nIt’s commonly included in **Railay half-day plans**.\n\n\n### Phra Nang Beach Tips for Visitors\n### \n- Carry cash for boats and snacks\n- Wear reef-safe sunscreen\n- Respect the cave shrine\n- Water shoes helpful at low tide\n- Avoid peak midday heat\n\n\n### Explore Railay & Krabi Beaches with India Tour Expeditions\n### \nAt **India Tour Expeditions**, we curate Krabi itineraries that balance beaches, culture and comfort for Indian travellers.\n\n✔️ **Phra Nang Beach & Railay tours**\n\n✔️ Ao Nang longtail boat arrangements\n\n✔️ Family-friendly Krabi sightseeing\n\n✔️ Krabi tour packages from India\n\n🏝️ Add **Phra Nang Beach** to your Thailand itinerary for one of Thailand’s most iconic beach experiences.",
