        "id": 429,
        "name": "Emerald Pool",
        "brief": "Natural Emerald Hot Spring Pool",
        "description": "**Emerald Pool Krabi**, locally known as **Sa Morakot**, is one of the most beautiful natural attractions in southern Thailand. Located inside the lush **Thung Teao Forest Natural Park**, **Emerald Pool Thailand** is famous for its crystal-clear turquoise water formed by natural mineral springs.\n\nOften combined with nearby hot springs, the **Krabi Emerald Pool hot spring** experience is perfect for travellers looking to enjoy nature, light adventure, and relaxation in one visit. The pool is fed by underground streams, giving it its striking green-blue colour, which changes with light and season.\n\nThis guide covers everything you need to know about visiting the **Emerald Pool Krabi**, including swimming rules, walking trails, nearby Blue Pool, how to reach, opening hours, and entry fee details.\n\n### Why Visit Emerald Pool in Krabi\n### \n- One of the most scenic **natural pools in Krabi**\n- Famous **emerald green and turquoise water**\n- Safe and refreshing **Emerald Pool swimming Krabi** experience\n- Located inside **Thung Teao Forest Emerald Pool**\n- Easy half-day trip from Ao Nang or Krabi Town\n- Ideal for nature lovers and families\n\nFor Indian travellers, Emerald Pool offers a calm, refreshing break from beaches and island hopping.\n\n\n### Emerald Pool Krabi Location & Background\n### \n📍 Located in **Thung Teao Forest Natural Park**, Krabi\n- Also known as **Sa Morakot Krabi**\n- Surrounded by protected rainforest and nature trails\n\nThe pool was formed naturally by mineral-rich hot springs flowing through limestone layers.\n\n\n### Swimming, Trails and Nearby Blue Pool\n### \nEmerald Pool is part of a larger forest area with multiple attractions.\n\n#### Nature Walks and Hot Spring Waters\n#### \nHighlights include:\n\n- Clear, cool water ideal for swimming\n- Natural **mineral hot springs in Krabi**\n- Shaded **jungle trail Emerald Pool Krabi** walk\n- Wooden walkways through the forest\n- Peaceful natural surroundings\n\nSwimming is allowed only in the Emerald Pool and **Crystal Pool Krabi**, not in the Blue Pool.\n\n#### Blue Pool Krabi Lagoon (Viewpoint Only)\n#### \n- Located deeper inside the forest\n- Known as **Blue Pool Krabi lagoon**\n- Intense deep-blue colour due to minerals\n- **Swimming not allowed** to protect the ecosystem\n\nThe Blue Pool is best visited early morning for colour and clarity.\n\n\n### Emerald Pool Krabi Opening Hours and Entry Fee\n### \n**Opening Days:**\n\n✔️ Open daily\n\n**Emerald Pool Krabi Opening Hours:**\n\n✔️ **9:00 AM – 5:00 PM**\n\n**Entrance Fee:**\n\n✔️ Entry fee applicable (separate charges for locals and tourists)\n\n Entry fees contribute to forest conservation and maintenance.\n\n\n### How to Reach Emerald Pool from Ao Nang or Krabi Town\n### \n- 🚗 Approx. **1–1.5 hours drive from Ao Nang**\n- Easily reachable by taxi or private transfer\n- Often included in **Emerald Pool Blue Pool hot springs tour**\n\nMany travellers search **how to reach Emerald Pool from Ao Nang Krabi**, as it is commonly done as a half-day trip.\n\n\n### Best Time to Visit Emerald Pool Krabi\n### \n**Best Season:**\n\n✔️ November to April (dry season)\n\n**Best Time of Day:**\n\n✔️ Early morning to avoid crowds\n\n✔️ Midday for warmer swimming water\n\nThe **best time to visit Emerald Pool during the dry season** offers clearer water and safer walking trails.\n\n\n### Emerald Pool Walking Trail Distance\n### \n- Main walking trail: approx. **800–1,400 metres**\n- Easy to moderate walk\n- Well-marked paths and wooden walkways\n\nThe **Emerald Pool Krabi walking trail distance** is manageable for most travellers.\n\n### Tips for Visiting Emerald Pool Krabi\n### \n- Wear comfortable walking shoes\n- Carry swimwear and towel\n- Avoid weekends if possible\n- Follow park rules strictly\n- Do not use sunscreen before swimming\n\nCombine Emerald Pool with nearby hot springs for a complete nature experience.\n\n\n### Explore Emerald Pool Krabi with India Tour Expeditions\n### \nAt **India Tour Expeditions**, we curate nature-based experiences for Indian travellers.\n\n✔️ **Emerald Pool Krabi tours**\n\n✔️ Blue Pool & hot springs combinations\n\n✔️ Private transfers from Ao Nang\n\n✔️ End-to-end Thailand travel planning\n\n🌿 Add **Emerald Pool Krabi (Sa Morakot)** to your Thailand itinerary and experience one of Thailand’s most beautiful natural lagoons.",
