        "id": 859,
        "name": "Aquaria Phuket",
        "brief": "Thailand’s Largest Aquarium with Marine Life",
        "description": "**Aquaria Phuket** is Thailand’s largest and most immersive aquarium experience, offering a fascinating journey through marine and freshwater ecosystems from around the world. Located inside **Central Phuket Floresta**, **Aquaria Phuket Thailand** is one of the top **family-friendly attractions in Phuket**, especially popular among travellers visiting with kids.\n\nHome to over **25,000 marine animals**, the **Aquaria Phuket aquarium** features massive tanks, underwater tunnels, and themed zones showcasing rivers, rainforests, coastal waters, and open seas. As a fully air-conditioned indoor attraction, it is ideal for travellers looking for **things to do in Phuket with kids indoors**, especially during hot afternoons or rainy days.\n\nThis guide covers everything you need to know about visiting **Aquaria Phuket**, including ticket details, opening hours, zones, feeding shows, and helpful tips for families.\n\nCheck Best of Thailand Itinerary here!\n\n### Why Visit Aquaria Phuket Thailand\n### \n- **Thailand’s largest aquarium** with world-class exhibits\n- Considered the **best aquarium in Phuket** for families\n- Ideal **indoor attraction in Phuket for kids**\n- Home to **over 25,000 marine animals**\n- Educational yet entertaining experience\n- Convenient location inside **Central Phuket Floresta aquarium complex**\n\nFor Indian travellers, Aquaria Phuket offers a comfortable, informative, and weather-proof sightseeing option.\n\n\n### Aquaria Phuket Location & Background\n### \n📍 **Central Phuket Floresta Mall, Phuket Town**\n- One of Southeast Asia’s largest aquarium complexes\n- Easily accessible from Patong, Kata, Karon, and Old Phuket Town\n\nAquaria Phuket was designed as a modern marine conservation and education centre, combining entertainment with awareness about aquatic ecosystems.\n\nVisit Bangkok and Pattaya with India Tour!\n\n### Aquaria Phuket Opening Hours\n### \n**Opening Days:**\n\n✔️ Open daily\n\n**Aquaria Phuket Opening Hours:**\n\n✔️ **10:30 AM – 7:00 PM**\n\n(last entry usually earlier in the evening)\n\n🕒 Visiting earlier in the day is recommended for a quieter experience, especially during school holidays.\n\n\n### Highlights of Aquaria Phuket\n### \nAquaria Phuket is divided into multiple themed zones and interactive experiences.\n\n\n#### Marine Life and Special Zones\n#### \nVisitors can explore carefully designed zones that represent different aquatic habitats:\n\n- **Mystic Forest** – Freshwater species inspired by rainforests and rivers\n- **River Caves** – Giant freshwater fish and river ecosystems\n- **Coastal Haven** – Tropical coastal marine life\n- **South China Sea** – Sharks, rays, and large open-ocean species\n\nThe aquarium showcases **over 25,000 marine animals at Aquaria Phuket**, including sharks, stingrays, jellyfish, turtles, and colourful reef fish. Highlights include **penguins and otters at Aquaria Phuket**, which are especially popular with children.\n\nDiscover Bangkok and Pattaya with Our Itinerary!\n\n#### Daily Feeding Shows and Educational Experiences\n#### \nLive feeding sessions and educational activities are a key highlight.\n\n- Scheduled **Aquaria Phuket feeding show timings** throughout the day\n- Penguin and otter feeding sessions\n- Shark and ray feeding demonstrations\n- Informative talks by trained marine staff\n\nThese experiences make Aquaria Phuket both educational and engaging for families.\n\n#### Aquaria Phuket Trick Eye Museum\n#### \nLocated in the same complex, the **Aquaria Phuket Trick Eye Museum** is a popular add-on experience.\n\n- Interactive 3D art and optical illusion exhibits\n- Fun photo opportunities for families and groups\n- Often combined with aquarium entry\n\nMany travellers opt for **Aquaria Phuket tickets with Trick Eye Museum** for a more complete indoor experience.\n\n\n### How to Reach Aquaria Phuket\n### \n- Easily reachable by taxi or private cab from major beach areas\n- Included in many Phuket city sightseeing tours\n- Located within a major shopping mall with dining options\n\nIts central location makes it easy to combine Aquaria Phuket with shopping or Old Phuket Town visits.\n\n\n### Tickets, Combos & Tips for Visiting with Family\n### \n**Aquaria Phuket tickets** vary depending on inclusions.\n\nTicket options may include:\n\n- Standard aquarium entry\n- **Aquaria Phuket tickets with Trick Eye Museum**\n- Family or combo passes\n\n### Travel Tips for Aquaria Phuket:\n\n- Ideal for **things to do in Phuket with kids indoors**\n- Allocate **1.5–2 hours** for the visit\n- Comfortable footwear recommended\n- Photography allowed in most areas (no flash)\n\n### Book Aquaria Phuket Tickets with India Tour Expeditions\n### \nAt **India Tour Expeditions**, we curate Phuket attractions for Indian travellers.\n\n✔️ **Aquaria Phuket tickets**\n\n✔️ Combo tickets with Trick Eye Museum\n\n✔️ Phuket city tours and family-friendly attractions\n\n✔️ Seamless planning and local support\n\n🐠 Add **Aquaria Phuket Thailand** to your Phuket itinerary and enjoy one of the country’s most impressive indoor attractions.",
