        "name": "Koh Kood Island",
        "brief": "Peaceful Island Escape with Waterfalls, Beaches & Clear Blue Seas",
        "description": "**Koh Kood Island Thailand**, also known as **Ko Kut Thailand**, is one of the country’s most unspoiled and peaceful island destinations. Located near the Cambodian border in eastern Thailand, **Koh Kood** is famous for its pristine white-sand beaches, crystal-clear turquoise waters, jungle-covered interiors, and relaxed fishing villages.\n\nUnlike party-centric islands, **Koh Kood untouched island** experiences focus on nature, slow travel, and local life. With very limited nightlife and minimal crowds, the island is ideal for travellers seeking tranquillity, scenic beauty, and a break from mass tourism.\n\nThis **Koh Kood travel guide** covers everything you need to know about planning a visit, including beaches, waterfalls, villages, how to reach the island, best season, and suggested itineraries.\n\n### Why Visit Koh Kood – Quiet Alternative to Busy Thai Islands\n### \n- One of Thailand’s most **untouched islands**\n- Quiet, crowd-free beaches and clear water\n- Lush jungle interiors with waterfalls\n- Authentic fishing villages and local life\n- Perfect for couples, families, and slow travellers\n- Minimal nightlife and no party scene\n\nFor Indian travellers seeking calm, scenic destinations, Koh Kood offers a refreshing alternative to busier islands like Phuket or Koh Samui.\n\n\n### Koh Kood Island Location & Background\n### \n📍 Located in **Trat Province**, eastern Thailand\n- Thailand’s fourth-largest island\n- Close to the Cambodia border\n\nThe island has remained largely undeveloped due to its remote location, preserving its natural charm.\n\n\n### Best Beaches on Koh Kood\n### \nKoh Kood is known for long, peaceful beaches with soft sand and shallow water.\n\n#### Klong Chao, Ao Tapao and Bang Bao Beaches\n#### \nTop beach spots include:\n\n- **Klong Chao Beach Koh Kood** – central, scenic, great for swimming\n- **Ao Tapao Beach sunset** views and calm atmosphere\n- **Bang Bao Beach** – quiet, resort-lined shoreline\n\nThe **Koh Kood beaches and waterfalls** combination makes the island perfect for relaxed exploration.\n\n### Waterfalls, Jungle Trails and Fishing Villages\n### \nBeyond beaches, Koh Kood offers lush inland experiences.\n\n#### Klong Chao Waterfall, Ao Salat Village and Island Interior\n#### \nMust-visit inland highlights:\n\n- **Klong Chao Waterfall Koh Kood** – freshwater pool surrounded by jungle\n- Short jungle trails and cycling routes\n- **Ao Salat fishing village Koh Kood** – stilt houses and traditional life\n- Coconut plantations and quiet rural roads\n\nThese attractions highlight the island’s authentic and laid-back character.\n\nCheck Our Thailand Packages here!\n\n### Snorkelling and Diving Near Koh Kood\n### \nWhile not as famous as Andaman islands, Koh Kood offers decent marine experiences.\n\n- Snorkelling around coral patches near beaches\n- Day trips to **Koh Rang Marine Park diving snorkelling** areas\n- Calm water conditions during dry season\n\n\n### Best Time to Visit Koh Kood Island\n### \n**Best Season:**\n\n✔️ **November to April** (dry season)\n\n**Green Season (May–Oct):**\n\n- Rough seas\n- Limited boat services\n- Heavy rainfall\n\n Most travellers prefer **best time to visit Koh Kood November to April**.\n\nPhuket and Krabi Tour package by India Tour Expeditions\n\n### How to Get to Koh Kood from Bangkok or Trat\n### \n- Travel from **Bangkok to Trat** (flight or road)\n- Boat transfer from **Laem Sok Pier, Trat**\n- Speedboat or ferry to Koh Kood\n\nTravellers often search **how to get to Koh Kood from Bangkok or Trat** due to the island’s remote access.\n\n\n### Koh Kood vs Koh Chang – Which Is Quieter\n### \n- **Koh Kood**: Much quieter, more natural, limited nightlife\n- **Koh Chang**: More developed, busier beaches\n\nKoh Kood is ideal for travellers seeking complete relaxation.\n\n\n### Suggested 3 Day Koh Kood Itinerary\n### \n**Day 1:**\n\n- Arrival and beach relaxation\n- Sunset at Ao Tapao\n\n**Day 2:**\n\n- Visit Klong Chao Waterfall\n- Explore Ao Salat fishing village\n\n**Day 3:**\n\n- Snorkelling or Koh Rang Marine Park trip\n- Leisure time before departure\n\n A **3 day itinerary Koh Kood beaches waterfalls fishing villages** is perfect for first-time visitors.\n\n\n### Tips for Visiting Koh Kood\n### \n- Carry cash (limited ATMs)\n- Book transfers in advance\n- Rent a scooter for easy exploration\n- Pack light rainwear during shoulder season\n- Respect local communities\n\n\n### Explore Koh Kood Island with India Tour Expeditions\n### \nAt **India Tour Expeditions**, we curate slow-travel island escapes for Indian travellers.\n\n✔️ **Koh Kood island tours & planning**\n\n✔️ Beach and nature-focused itineraries\n\n✔️ Thailand tour packages from India\n\n🌊 Add **Koh Kood Island Thailand** to your Thailand itinerary and experience one of the country’s last untouched island paradises.",
