        "name": "Fisherman's Village",
        "brief": "Charming Beachside Village",
        "description": "**Fisherman’s Village Koh Samui** is one of the island’s most charming and atmospheric areas, located along **Bophut Beach** on the northern coast. Known for its preserved wooden shophouses, beachfront restaurants, and lively walking street, **Fisherman’s Village Thailand** blends traditional island charm with relaxed nightlife.\n\nThe highlight of the area is the **Fisherman’s Village Walking Street**, which comes alive every Friday evening as a vibrant night market. With street food, handicrafts, live music, and fire shows by the beach, **Bophut Fisherman’s Village** is especially popular among families, couples, and travellers looking for a laid-back alternative to Chaweng’s party scene.\n\nThis guide covers everything you need to know about visiting **Fisherman’s Village Koh Samui**, including the Friday night market, dining options, how to reach, and evening tips.\n\n\n### Why Visit Fisherman’s Village in Koh Samui\n### \n- One of the most charming areas in Koh Samui\n- Famous **Fisherman’s Village night market Friday**\n- Relaxed, scenic alternative to busy nightlife zones\n- Excellent **Fisherman’s Village seafood dining**\n- Ideal **family-friendly Fisherman’s Village market**\n- Beautiful seaside setting at **Bophut Beach**\n\nFor Indian travellers, Fisherman’s Village offers culture, food, and evening entertainment without loud clubbing.\n\n\n### Fisherman’s Village Koh Samui Location & Background\n### \n📍 Located at **Bophut Beach**, north Koh Samui\n- One of the island’s oldest settlements\n- Preserved Sino-Thai style wooden buildings\n\nOnce home to fishing communities, the area has been carefully restored into a cultural and dining hub.\n\nCheck Our Best of Thailand itinerary here\n\n### Friday Night Market and Beachfront Vibes\n### \nThe **Fisherman’s Village Walking Street** is the main attraction.\n\n#### Street Food, Shops and Performances\n#### \nWhat to expect on Friday evenings:\n\n- Local Thai street food and snacks\n- **Walking street handicrafts Samui** and souvenirs\n- Beachfront cafés and cocktail bars\n- Live music and acoustic performances\n- **Fire shows at Fisherman’s Village Beach**\n\nThe **Fisherman’s Village opening hours on Friday** usually start around **5:00 PM** and continue late into the night.\n\nDiscover Bangkok and Pattaya on your vacation\n\n### Best Time to Visit Fisherman’s Village\n### \n**Best Day:**\n\n✔️ Friday (for the walking street market)\n\n**Best Time:**\n\n✔️ 6:00 PM onwards for food and atmosphere\n\nEven on non-market days, the area is lively in the evenings with restaurants and bars open along the beach.\n\n### Location on Bophut Beach and How to Reach\n### \n- Easily reachable by taxi or songthaew\n- Approx. **15 minutes from Chaweng**\n- Around **10 minutes from Koh Samui Airport**\n\nMany travellers search **how to reach Bophut Fisherman’s Village Samui**, as it is centrally located and easy to access.\n\n\n### Dining Tips and Evening Guide\n### \n- Reserve tables in advance for beachfront restaurants\n- Try fresh seafood at **best restaurants in Fisherman’s Village Koh Samui**\n- Visit during sunset for the best views\n- Comfortable for families with children and seniors\n\nWhen comparing nightlife, **Fisherman’s Village vs Chaweng nightlife**—Fisherman’s Village is relaxed and cultural, while Chaweng is energetic and party-focused.\n\n### Explore Fisherman’s Village with India Tour Expeditions\n### \nAt **India Tour Expeditions**, we curate Koh Samui experiences for Indian travellers.\n\n✔️ Koh Samui sightseeing & evening walks\n\n✔️ Fisherman’s Village night market visits\n\n✔️ Koh Samui tour packages from India\n\n✔️ End-to-end Thailand travel planning\n\n🌴 Add **Fisherman’s Village Koh Samui** to your Thailand itinerary and enjoy one of the island’s most charming evening destinations.",
