        "name": "The Mud Crabs Sculpture",
        "brief": "Iconic Krabi Landmark Featuring Giant Mud Crab Sculptures",
        "description": "The **Mud Crabs Sculpture Krabi**, locally known as **Lan Pu Dam**, is one of the most recognisable **Krabi Town landmarks** and a favourite stop for photos along the riverfront. This striking **black crab sculpture** features a **mother mud crab with three baby crabs**, symbolising Krabi’s strong connection to fishing traditions, mangroves, and coastal life.\n\nSet beside the **Krabi River estuary** near **Khanap Nam Pier**, the sculpture offers beautiful views of the water and the iconic **Khao Khanap Nam mountains** in the background. It’s a quick, free stop that fits perfectly into an evening walk around Krabi Town.\n\n\n### Why See the Mud Crabs Sculpture\n### \n- One of the most famous **Krabi Town landmarks**\n- Symbol of local **fishing culture & mangrove ecosystems**\n- Easy, **free photo spot** by the river\n- Scenic backdrop with limestone mountains\n- Walking distance from **Krabi Walking Street & Night Market**\n\nFor travellers exploring Krabi Town beyond beaches, this is a simple but meaningful stop.\n\nBest of Thailand with India Tour Expeditions\n\n### Location at Khanap Nam Pier & Photo Opportunities\n### \n📍 **Lan Pu Dam, Krabi Town**\n\n📍 Near **Khanap Nam Pier** on the riverfront\n\n**What Makes the Location Special**\n\n-  Views of the **Krabi River estuary**\n-  Clear sight of **Khao Khanap Nam twin mountains**\n- Boats heading into mangrove channels\n- Beautiful light during sunset\n\nMany visitors search **mud crabs sculpture Krabi town location and photos**, and sunset is when the sculpture truly stands out.\n\n\n### Khao Khanap Nam Mountains & River Estuary Vibe\n### \nJust behind the sculpture, you’ll see the dramatic **Khao Khanap Nam mountains**, often considered the gateway to Krabi Town. The calm river, mangroves, and passing longtail boats create a relaxed, local atmosphere — very different from Ao Nang’s tourist buzz.\n\nThis area also serves as a departure point for **mangrove and cave boat tours**.\n\n\n### Nearby Attractions – Night Market, Walking Street & Mangroves\n### \nThe sculpture is ideally placed for combining multiple Krabi Town experiences.\n\n**What’s Nearby**\n\n-  **Krabi Town Night Market / Walking Street** (short walk)\n-  **Chao Fah Park** riverside area\n-  **Mangrove & cave boat tours** from Khanap Nam Pier\n-  Local food stalls and cafés\n\nMany travellers plan a short walking route from **Krabi Walking Street to the Mud Crabs Sculpture**, making it an easy evening plan.\n\nPlan your family vacation to Thailand\n\n### Best Time to Visit & Quick Tips\n### \n✔️ **Best time:** Late afternoon to sunset\n\n✔️ **Visit duration:** 10–20 minutes\n\n✔️ **Entry fee:** Free\n\n✔️ **Photography:** Best with wide-angle lens\n\n✔️ **Footwear:** Comfortable walking shoes\n\nIf you’re visiting the night market, stop here **before or after dinner** for the best experience.\n\n\n### Walking Route from Krabi Town Center\n### \n- Start at **Krabi Walking Street**\n- Walk towards **Chao Fah Park**\n- Continue along the river to **Khanap Nam Pier**\n- Reach **Lan Pu Dam (Mud Crabs Sculpture)**\n\nThis short route covers some of the most atmospheric parts of Krabi Town.\n\n\n### Add Mud Crabs Sculpture to Your Krabi Town Walk with India Tour Expeditions\n### \nAt **India Tour Expeditions**, we help Indian travellers discover local highlights beyond typical beach itineraries.\n\n✔️ Krabi Town evening walks\n\n✔️ Night market & street food experiences\n\n✔️ Mangrove boat tours from Khanap Nam Pier\n\n✔️ Krabi sightseeing itineraries\n\nThe **Mud Crabs Sculpture Krabi** is a small stop — but it perfectly captures the soul of Krabi Town.\n\nStart planning your Thailand Trip now!",
