        "location": "Private Trip",
        "routeSummary": "",
        "overviewText": "We have perfected this Meghalaya route over years of exploration. \n\nWe know exactly what makes Meghalaya worth the flight. Here is our signature handcrafted expedition. Six days. One small group. Every part of Meghalaya that's actually worth your time.\n\nWe start you off in Shillong. The hills fold into pine forests here. Markets stay busy till evening.\n\nDay two, we take you to Laitlum Canyon. It's one of our favourite stops on the whole trip. You'll stand at the edge. Watch clouds drift through a valley that just drops away.\n\nThen it's on to Cherrapunji. One of the wettest places on the planet. You'll understand why the moment the mist rolls in.\n\nDay three is the one people talk about for years. We trek you down to the Double Decker Living Root Bridge. It's grown by hand over generations. Still holding strong today. Seven Sisters Falls roars nearby. Especially heavy if you catch it post-monsoon.\n\nFrom there, we slow things down. Dawki's Umngot river is that still. That clear. Boats look like they're floating on glass.\n\nMawlynnong comes next. Known as Asia's cleanest village. Bamboo pathways, hidden root bridges tucked into the trees.\n\nBy day six, we're driving you back to Guwahati. Tired legs. Better photos than you planned for. A group of near-strangers who feel like old friends by now.\n\n**Explore Meghalaya Itineraries**\n\n### 📍 Meghalaya Places We'll Take You To\n### \n1. **Shillong:** Meghalaya's capital. Your base for the first two days. The hills here fold straight into pine forest. Local markets stay open till late. Cafes, bakeries, live music spots too. It's the easiest place to settle into Meghalaya's pace.\n2. **Laitlum Canyon:** A cliffside viewpoint we save for golden hour. The name means \"end of hills\" in Khasi. And it feels exactly like that. The valley just drops away below you. Clouds move through it in real time. One of the quietest, least crowded views on the whole route.\n3. **Cherrapunji:** One of the wettest places on Earth. Locally known as Sohra. Waterfalls, caves, and root bridge country, all packed into one region. The landscape changes fast here. Mist rolls in within minutes, then clears just as quick.\n4. **Double Decker Living Root Bridge:** A two-tier bridge grown from rubber tree roots. Built by hand, over generations. Locals still use it to cross the river below. We trek you there through Cherrapunji's forest trails. Steps, streams, dense green canopy the whole way.\n5. **Seven Sisters Falls:** A multi-tiered waterfall, seven streams falling together. Best seen right after monsoon, when the flow's heaviest. You view it from a lookout point across the valley. On a clear day, you can see it from a real distance.\n6. **Mawsmai Cave:** A limestone cave near Cherrapunji. Short, walkable, no technical gear needed. Narrow passages, natural light breaking in through gaps above. Takes about 20-30 minutes end to end. A good break between the bigger trekking days.\n7. **Mawlynnong:** Asia's cleanest village, and it earns that title. Bamboo walkways run through the whole settlement. A living root bridge sits right on the edge of the village. Climb the bamboo skywalk for a treetop view of the plains below, all the way into Bangladesh on a clear day.\n8. **Dawki:** Home to the Umngot river. Famous for water so still and clear, it looks like glass from above. Boats seem to float in mid-air in photos. This is also where we base you for water activities.\n9. **Krang Suri / Phe Phe Falls:** A turquoise-pool waterfall, tucked away from the main tourist trail. Photogenic, and rarely crowded. The pool below is calm enough to swim in. A good last stop before you head back toward Guwahati.\n\nWant to add Kaziranga? **Check this Meghalaya Trip**\n\n### ✅ Things To Do In Meghalaya On This Trip\n### \n✓ Trek to the Double Decker Living Root Bridge through Cherrapunji's forest trails\n\n✓ Cliff jump into the Umngot river at Dawki\n\n✓ Snorkel in Dawki's clear river water\n\n✓ Take a boat ride across the calmest river you'll ever see\n\n✓ Explore Mawsmai Cave's limestone passages\n\n✓ Sit around a bonfire by the river at Dawki\n\n✓ Catch sunrise or sunset from Laitlum Canyon\n\n\n### Why Experience Meghalaya With India Tour\n\n- **We've packed in all the highlights:** Root bridges, waterfalls, caves, the Umngot river. One trip. Seamlessly organized from airport to airport.\n- **You get built-in company:** Small group format means new people. Split costs too. None of the awkward solo-trip logistics.\n- **We handle everything:** Stays, transport, permits, entry fees. A certified India Tour trip leader accompanying you throughout. You simply immerse yourself and enjoy.\n- **We balance the pace right:** Real trekking days. Slower sightseeing days too. Nobody's wiped out by day three.\n\n**Inquire for your Meghalaya Trip**",
