    "faqs": [
      {
        "id": 5871,
        "question": "How to reach Meghalaya from major Indian cities?",
        "answer": "The easiest way to reach Meghalaya is by flying to Guwahati, which is the main gateway for most travellers. From Guwahati, Shillong is around 3 hours by road. Trains to Guwahati are also available from major Indian cities.\n\nLet India Tour curate your [Meghalaya Trip!",
        "group": "All"
      },
      {
        "id": 5872,
        "question": "Which is better to stay in – Shillong or Cherrapunji?",
        "answer": "Both offer different experiences. Shillong is better for hotels, cafes, shopping, and central connectivity. Cherrapunji is better for waterfalls, scenic resorts, and nature stays. Many travellers split their stay between both.",
        "group": "All"
      },
      {
        "id": 5873,
        "question": "Is Meghalaya safe for tourists?",
        "answer": "Yes, Meghalaya is considered one of the safer tourist destinations in India for couples, families, and solo travellers. Locals are generally warm and welcoming.",
        "group": "All"
      },
      {
        "id": 5874,
        "question": "How many days are enough for Meghalaya?",
        "answer": "A 5 to 7 day trip is ideal to cover Shillong, Cherrapunji, Dawki, Mawlynnong, and nearby attractions comfortably.\n\nCheck Our Meghalaya Group Trip Here!",
        "group": "All"
      },
      {
        "id": 5875,
        "question": "Do Indian travellers need a permit for Meghalaya?",
        "answer": "No, Indian citizens usually do not need any permit to visit Meghalaya. Carry a valid government ID for hotel check-ins.",
        "group": "All"
      },
      {
        "id": 5876,
        "question": "Is Meghalaya expensive?",
        "answer": "Meghalaya suits all budgets. You can plan a budget trip with shared cabs and homestays or choose premium resorts and private transport.",
        "group": "All"
      },
      {
        "id": 5877,
        "question": "Can I visit Kaziranga along with Meghalaya?",
        "answer": "Yes. Guwahati connects both, so you can cover Kaziranga's wildlife and Meghalaya's hills in a single trip without a major detour.",
        "group": "All"
      },
      {
        "id": 5880,
        "question": "What is the best time to visit Kaziranga with Meghalaya?\n",
        "answer": "November to April works best for both, Kaziranga safaris are open and Meghalaya's skies are at their clearest.\n\n**Plan your Meghalaya Tour with India Tour today!**",
        "group": "All"
      },
      {
        "id": 5884,
        "question": "How far is Kaziranga from Guwahati?",
        "answer": "Around 4 hours by road, making it an easy add-on before or after your Meghalaya leg.",
        "group": "All"
      },
      {
        "id": 5878,
        "question": "What is Meghalaya famous for?",
        "answer": "Meghalaya is famous for living root bridges, waterfalls, caves, crystal-clear rivers, clean villages, and misty hill landscapes.",
        "group": "All"
      },
      {
        "id": 5879,
        "question": "What is the best time to visit Meghalaya?",
        "answer": "The best time to visit Meghalaya is October to April for clear weather and sightseeing. Monsoon is best for lush greenery and waterfalls.",
        "group": "All"
      },
      {
        "id": 5881,
        "question": "Is Meghalaya good for honeymoon?",
        "answer": "Absolutely. Meghalaya is peaceful, scenic, and romantic, making it perfect for couples looking for waterfalls, cosy stays, road trips, and quiet nature escapes.",
        "group": "All"
      },
      {
        "id": 5882,
        "question": "Is vegetarian food available in Meghalaya?",
        "answer": "Yes, vegetarian food is easily available in Shillong, Cherrapunji, and popular tourist towns. You can find North Indian, South Indian, café food, and basic Jain-friendly options in some places.",
        "group": "All"
      },
      {
        "id": 5883,
        "question": "Can I visit Dawki in one day from Shillong?",
        "answer": "Yes, Dawki is commonly visited as a day trip from Shillong. Many travellers combine Dawki with Mawlynnong on the same day.",
        "group": "All"
      },
      {
        "id": 5885,
        "question": "What should I pack for Meghalaya?",
        "answer": "Carry comfortable shoes, a light jacket, rainwear, medicines, power bank, and some cash for remote areas. Weather can change quickly, so layered clothing is always a smart choice.",
        "group": "All"
      },
      {
        "id": 5886,
        "question": "Is Meghalaya good during monsoon?",
        "answer": "Yes, monsoon is one of the most beautiful times to visit Meghalaya. Waterfalls are at full strength, valleys turn lush green, and clouds create dramatic landscapes. Just keep buffer time for rain-related travel delays.",
        "group": "All"
      },
      {
        "id": 5887,
        "question": "Is mobile network available in Meghalaya?",
        "answer": "Mobile network works well in Shillong and larger towns, but can be weak in remote villages, caves, and trekking areas. Download maps in advance before long road trips.",
        "group": "All"
      }
    ],
