    "tagline": "Discover private overwater villas, crystal turquoise lagoons, vibrant coral reefs and luxury island retreats in the Maldives.",
    "about": "### **Why Visit The Maldives**\nThe Maldives is a tropical paradise in the Indian Ocean, famous for crystal-clear turquoise waters, pristine white-sand sandbanks, and iconic luxury overwater bungalows. Comprising 26 natural atolls and over 1,000 coral islands, it is one of the world's premier destinations for couples, honeymooners, divers, and marine life lovers.\n\n- **Private Overwater Bungalows** – Wake up with direct steps into warm, calm turquoise lagoons and panoramic ocean sunsets.\n- **World-Class Marine Life** – Snorkel and scuba dive alongside gentle nurse sharks, sea turtles, manta rays, and colorful reef fish.\n- **Visa on Arrival for Indians** – Free 30-day tourist visa granted upon arrival at Velana International Airport (Male).\n- **Romantic Beach Dining** – Enjoy candlelit beach dinners under starlit skies and floating breakfasts in your private pool.\n- **Convenient Speedboat & Seaplane Transfers** – Seamless, scenic arrivals from Male directly to your island resort jetty.\n\n### **Best Time to Visit the Maldives**\n- **Peak Season (November to April):** Dry, sunny weather with calm seas, maximum water visibility (over 30 meters), perfect for snorkeling, diving, and beach lovers.\n- **Monsoon & Value Season (May to October):** Warm tropical weather with occasional rain showers, lush island foliage, fewer crowds, and the best resort discount deals.\n\n### **How to Reach the Maldives**\nDirect non-stop flights operate daily to **Velana International Airport (Male - MLE)** from major Indian metro hubs:\n- Mumbai to Male: ~2.5 hours\n- Delhi to Male: ~4 hours\n- Bengaluru / Kochi to Male: ~1.5 to 2 hours\nUpon arrival in Male, our airport representative escorts you to your resort speedboat or seaplane terminal.",
